precept PaymentMethod

# A stateless data-only precept governing a single stored payment method.
# A payment method holds the verified card details and the lightweight
# cardholder-controlled flags (nickname, default selection). The card data
# itself is immutable once stored — re-storing requires creating a new record.
#
# The verified payment instrument fields (LastFour, ExpiryMonth, ExpiryYear,
# CardholderName, CardBrand) are caller-supplied at storage. IsDefault and
# Nickname are display-layer preferences the cardholder can change after the
# card is saved; the host application is responsible for refusing edits to
# the instrument fields after the card-on-file is verified.

field CardholderName as string optional maxlength 200 editable
field LastFour as string optional maxlength 4 editable
field CardBrand as choice of string("Visa","Mastercard","Amex","Discover","JCB","UnionPay","Other") default "Other" editable
field ExpiryMonth as integer default 1 min 1 max 12 editable
field ExpiryYear as integer default 2025 min 2025 max 2099 editable

field IsDefault as boolean default false editable
field Nickname as string optional maxlength 50 editable

rule LastFour.length == 4 when LastFour is set because "LastFour {LastFour} must be exactly four digits — the field stores the last four characters of the PAN as a display string"
